From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: armada <armada@localhost>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(manager): whitelist Nebel virtual touchscreen

NebelOS runs a userspace daemon that creates a rotated internal-panel
pass-through uinput touchscreen node named "Nebel Trackpad Screen". It
lives under /devices/virtual/input, so Manager::run's "input" subsystem
branch discards it as a virtual device before composite device configs
(01-retroid-controller.yaml) can claim it as a touchscreen source:
"Nebel Trackpad Screen (eventN) is virtual, skipping consideration".

The node is virtual but explicitly created by us to be managed by
InputPlumber, so add its name to VIRT_DEVICE_WHITELIST alongside the
existing Sunshine virtual pad entries.
---
 src/input/manager.rs | 5 ++++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/src/input/manager.rs
+++ b/src/input/manager.rs
@@ -65,6 +65,11 @@
     "Sunshine gamepad (virtual) motion sensors",
     "Sunshine Nintendo (virtual) pad",
     "MSI WMI hotkeys",
+    // NebelOS: rotated internal-panel pass-through uinput node, created by our
+    // userspace daemon and matched as a touchscreen source by
+    // 01-retroid-controller.yaml. It is virtual but explicitly created by us
+    // to be managed by InputPlumber.
+    "Nebel Trackpad Screen",
 ];
 
 #[derive(Error, Debug)]
